    {
      "filename": "A second section of the Morrison Mural. (9d9b83eb-1dd8-b71b-0bae-bb53b61b3c4b).jpg",
      "title": "File:A second section of the Morrison Mural. (9d9b83eb-1dd8-b71b-0bae-bb53b61b3c4b).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/A_second_section_of_the_Morrison_Mural._%289d9b83eb-1dd8-b71b-0bae-bb53b61b3c4b%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_second_section_of_the_Morrison_Mural._(9d9b83eb-1dd8-b71b-0bae-bb53b61b3c4b).jpg",
      "width": 8200,
      "height": 5606,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "National Park Service",
      "description": "Another section of the Morrison Mural showing a portion of the river.\nThis section of the Morrison Mural shows the artists portrayal of an adult and juvenile Camarasaurus, a Camptosaurus and a Torvosaurus along with other animals of the Late Jurassic.  The two striped dinosaurs in the center of the picture represent Camarasaurus lentus.  You can see a Camarasaurus lentus skull, as found in the wall of bones, a few pictures back in this series.\nThis mural shows what we know about the Morrison environment, based on years of research by paleontologists and geologists.\nKeywords: torvosaurus; camptosaurus; camarasaurus; jurassic; mural; morrison; paleontologists; geologists",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 29 September 2011",
